-- title:
--   Locally Γ'-related Deligne data at translated chart points
-- statement:
--   The statement is set in the Čerednik–Drinfeld situation, with the following data and hypotheses.
--
--   **Coefficients.** A prime $r$; a commutative domain $\mathcal{O}$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), complete for the $\pi$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), with residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and with $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); and a field $K_0$ of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** A commutative domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of characteristic zero, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: completeness for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); maximality of that ideal (`hOnr_max`); every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) such that $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some $u\in\mathcal{O}^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma\colon G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma\le G$ such that: some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`); some $w\in\Gamma$ has $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`); and a subgroup $\Gamma'\le G$ consisting exactly of those $x\in\Gamma$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). Furthermore a homomorphism $\rho\colon G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ which is $\sigma$ followed by the projection (`hρ`), such that for every vertex $v$ of the lattice tree of $\mathcal{O}$ in $K_0$ the set of elements of $\rho(\Gamma')$ fixing $v$ is finite (`hdisc`), and there is a finite set $S$ of vertices with every vertex carried into $S$ by some element of $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The tower.** An element $g_1\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ whose matrix is $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`); a subgroup $N\le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`) which is normal in $\rho(\Gamma)$ (`hNnorm`) and of non-zero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`); and a Mumford tower $DM$ of type `MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, consisting of schemes $Z_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ with cartesian transition maps, proper and flat structure maps, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and a system of points $DM.q$ attached functorially to Deligne data over $\mathcal{O}$-algebras killed by $\pi^{n+1}$, invariant under $N$-pullback, together with its chart data.
--
--   **The intermediate tower with its $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed factor.** Schemes $X_n$ with structure maps $xb_n$ to $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ and transition maps $xt_n\colon X_n\to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G_2$ acting by automorphisms $a_n$ on each $X_n$; maps $pr_{1,n}\colon X_n\to Z_n$ and $pr_{2,n}\colon X_n\to\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$, where $\mathcal{O}_2$ denotes the equaliser of $\mathrm{Fr}\circ\mathrm{Fr}$ and the identity on $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (its $\mathrm{Fr}^2$-fixed subalgebra); a homomorphism $\theta\colon\Gamma\to G_2$; and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphisms $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ of $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$. The hypotheses on these data are: the transition squares are cartesian over the quotient maps $\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+2}\to\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1}$ (`hcart`); $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`); finite subsets of $X_n$ lie in affine opens (`haff`); the $G_2$-action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transitions (`ha_xt`); each $X_n$ is, via $pr_{1,n}$ and $pr_{2,n}$, the fibre product of $Z_n$ and $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1})$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ (`hX`), with $xb_n$ equal to $pr_{1,n}$ followed by $DM.zb_n$ (`hxb`), and with the transitions compatible with both projections (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`); $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) with $\theta\gamma=1$ if and only if $\rho\gamma\in N$ (`hθker`); $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}$ is induced by $\mathrm{Fr}$ on $\mathcal{O}_2$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ (`hFr₂`); the automorphism $a_n(\theta\gamma)$ acts on the second factor by $\mathrm{Fr}_{2,n}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ (`ha_pr₂`); and on the first factor it carries a point with $DM$-datum $P$ to one with datum $P'$ whenever $P'$ is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of $P$ (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   **The quotient datum.** A tower quotient datum $DQ$ for $(X,xb,xt,G_2,a)$, with quotient schemes $Y_n$ and maps $p_n\colon X_n\to Y_n$; and a system of points $q$ attaching to each pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (for $B$ an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with $\pi^{n+1}=0$) a morphism $\mathrm{Spec}\,B\to Y_n$, subject to: $q$ is computed by composing with $p_n$ any point of $X_n$ whose two projections are given by the Deligne datum and by the induced map on $\mathcal{O}_2/\pi^{n+1}$ (`hqdef`); $q$ lies over the structure map of $B$ (`hqover`); $q$ is natural in $B$ (`hqnat`); $q$ is compatible with the transitions $yt_n$ (`hqyt`); and $q$ is invariant under the twisted action of $\sigma\gamma$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma$, where two pairs are so related when the first components differ by precomposition with $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\sigma\gamma)}$ and the second is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of the first (`hqinv`).
--
--   **The unramified layer.** A presentation $Pr$ of type `MumfordTower.NrPresentation` for the above data, with subgroup $\theta(\Gamma'\cap\Gamma)$ of $G_2$, consisting of schemes $X'_n$ over $\mathrm{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})$, a $G_2$-action $a'$, maps $qX_n\colon X'_n\to X_n$ making the base-change squares cartesian, and chart morphisms $\kappa'_{h,n}$ from the spectrum of the edge chart ring $A_n(O^{\mathrm{nr}})$, the quotient of `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` by the ideal generated by the $(n+1)$-st power of $\pi$, to $X'_n$; a tower quotient datum $D'$ for $(Pr.X',Pr.xb',Pr.xt',G_2,Pr.a')$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; and comparison morphisms $rY_n\colon D'.Y_n\to DQ.Y_n$ making the squares over $\mathrm{Spec}(O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi^{n+1})\to\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/\pi^{n+1})$ cartesian (`hrY`), with $D'.p_n$ followed by $rY_n$ equal to $qX_n$ followed by $DQ.p_n$ (`hrY_p`) and with $rY$ compatible with the transitions (`hrY_yt`).
--
--   **The local situation.** An element $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$; a natural number $m$; a commutative ring $B$ which is both an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and an $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra compatibly, with $\pi^{m+1}=0$ in $B$ (`hB`); two $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra maps $\bar x,\bar x'\colon A_m(O^{\mathrm{nr}})\to B$; and four Deligne data $d,d',P,P'$ over $B$ relative to $K_0$ and $\pi$. The hypothesis `hd` has three clauses: the line of $d$ at the standard full lattice is the $B$-span of $\bar x(\xi)\otimes e_0+1\otimes e_1$ (where $\xi$ is the distinguished element `chartERing.ξ` read modulo $\pi^{m+1}$, and $e_0,e_1$ are the standard basis vectors of the standard lattice); the line of $d$ at $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ is the image under the base-changed action of $g_1$ of the $B$-span of $1\otimes e_0+\bar x(\eta)\otimes e_1$ (with $\eta$ the distinguished element `chartERing.η`); and $d$ lies in the edge chart for the pair $(g_1\cdot\text{std},\text{std})$, that is, for every prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $B$: $g_1\cdot\text{std}\subseteq\text{std}$, $\pi\cdot\text{std}\subseteq g_1\cdot\text{std}$, no $v$ in the standard lattice outside $g_1\cdot\text{std}$ has $1\otimes v$ in the line at the standard lattice plus $\mathfrak{p}$ times everything, and no $v'$ in $g_1\cdot\text{std}$ that is not $\pi$ times an element of the standard lattice has $1\otimes v'$ in the line at $g_1\cdot\text{std}$ plus $\mathfrak{p}$ times everything. The hypothesis `hd'` is the same for $d'$ and $\bar x'$. Moreover $P$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$ and $P'$ the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d'$ (`hP`, `hP'`): for every full lattice $M$, the line of $P$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $d$ at $h^{-1}\cdot M$ under the base-changed action of $h^{-1}$, and likewise for $P'$ and $d'$. Finally, an element $g\in G_2$ such that $\mathrm{Spec}(\bar x)$ followed by $\kappa'_{h,m}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}(\bar x')$ followed by $\kappa'_{h,m}$ followed by $Pr.a'_m(g)$ (`hpt`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a finite type $\iota$ and a family $f\colon\iota\to B$ such that the ideal generated by the range of $f$ is the whole of $B$, and such that for every $i\in\iota$ and every commutative ring $C$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra and a $B$-algebra compatibly and is a localisation of $B$ away from $f(i)$, there exists $\gamma\in\Gamma'$ for which the base change of $P'$ to $C$ is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of the base change of $P$ to $C$; explicitly, writing $P_C$ and $P'_C$ for the images of $P$ and $P'$ under the map of Deligne data induced by $B\to C$, for every full lattice $M$ the line of $P'_C$ at $M$ is the preimage of the line of $P_C$ at $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}\cdot M$ under the base-changed action of $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$. The element $\gamma$ is allowed to depend on $i$ and on $C$.
--
--   This is the local comparison step in the chart analysis of the unramified layer of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: two points of the edge chart of $X'_m$ whose images agree after translation by an element of the finite group $G_2$ have Deligne data that become related by an element of $\Gamma'$ after passing to a Zariski cover of the base. It is used in the proof of the overlap-agreement statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_overlap_agreement`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.descendedQuotientMap_nrFunctions_overlap_agreement) for the same tower.
